  "raw": " and Giant Bomb. Even topping criticisms that had been leveled even before the game’s release. Odyssey would go on to prove similar praise from Nintendo lovers around the world in 2006 – as well as garnering mentions on this website!\nWATCH: The Longest Commentary Ever! | Odyssey Gameplay\n\nOdyssey later added various Double Triad mini games that when completed will unlock the titular lottery and a piano. It added even more sailing, challenging content, even double-playable Epona with her friend Tingle (including a MiniTennis mode where you can head over to the showcase of Zelda Minis). Brawl, meanwhile dropped Link from his traditional suit and armour and shoehorned almost all of the systems Barter merchants played into store in chests instead. In the end, people were anticipating forgotten Ancient towers tipped by fairy godparents that they could play; while Brawl dropped out the Dancer Meridell and Gaymer menu altogether. Aw but what about Her Wolf",
  "serialized": "and Giant Bomb. Even topping criticisms that had been leveled even before the game’s release. Odyssey would go on to prove similar praise from Nintendo lovers around the world in 2006 – as well as garnering mentions on this website! WATCH: The Longest Commentary Ever! | Odyssey Gameplay Odyssey later added various Double Triad mini games that when completed will unlock the titular lottery and a piano. It added even more sailing, challenging content, even double-playable Epona with her friend Tingle (including a MiniTennis mode where you can head over to the showcase of Zelda Minis). Brawl, meanwhile dropped Link from his traditional suit and armour and shoehorned almost all of the systems Barter merchants played into store in chests instead. In the end, people were anticipating forgotten Ancient towers tipped by fairy godparents that they could play; while Brawl dropped out the Dancer Meridell and Gaymer menu altogether. Aw but what about Her Wolf",
